       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error, so I want to check with you first.\n\n**The problem:** Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg/day. Adults usually start at 5 mg daily (2.5 mg if frail, elderly or in liver impairment) and go up to 10 mg at most. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and fluid buildup, and calcium channel blocker overdose is hard to reverse.\n\n**Possible mix-ups:**\n- **5 mg** amlodipine, if a decimal point or extra zero slipped in\n- A different drug where 50 mg is a normal dose, such as **atenolol 50 mg** or **losartan 50 mg**\n\nPlease let me know which you meant:\n1. Amlodipine **5 mg** by mouth once daily\n2. Amlodipine **10 mg** by mouth once daily\n3. A different drug or dose\n4. Amlodipine 50 mg as written, if it's intentional. In that case, please give a clinical reason so I can document it on the order.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
