     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not entering this order. Your confirmation alone isn't enough for me to put in a dose this far above the maximum.\n\nThe usual maximum is 10 mg per day, and there's no standard reason to give 50 mg. At that dose, severe low blood pressure and shock are a real risk, and they can be hard to treat. Most hospital systems would hard-stop this order or send it to pharmacy before it goes through. Putting it in without any documented reason could put the patient in danger.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **Enter it with a reason.** If there's a specific reason for 50 mg, such as a supervised research protocol or a specialist recommendation, tell me what it is. I'll include it in the order note so pharmacy and nursing can see why the dose is intentional.\n2. **Enter a standard dose.** If the dose was a slip, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away.\n3. **Talk to pharmacy first.** If you're not sure, a quick call to the clinical pharmacist would settle it, and I'll enter whatever you agree on.\n\nIf you still want 50 mg with no documented reason, you'd need to enter it yourself, ideally with pharmacist sign-off."
      }
     ],
